    "description": {
      "value": "Investigation complete. All evidence collected, statements recorded, forensic reports received. Prima facie case well established against accused Amit Verma for offences under Section 281 BNS (Rash driving), Section 125 BNS (Act endangering life), Section 184 MV Act (Dangerous driving), and Section 134 MV Act (Failure to provide medical aid - accused did not actively assist victim though he was also injured, however the attempt to leave initially constitutes violation). Evidence list finalized - 15 exhibits. Case diary complete with 15 entries. All documents compiled and indexed in Annexures. Investigation reveals: Accused was overspeeding (52-58 kmph in 40 kmph zone), ignored traffic constable's manual stop signal, was in hurry to meet food delivery deadline, and due to high speed could not stop in time to avoid collision with victim's scooter who was making a legal turn at appropriate speed. Victim suffered grievous injuries requiring 36 days hospitalization and may have permanent disability. No contributory negligence by victim. Accused has no criminal history but his actions show disregard for traffic rules and public safety. Prepared final investigation report recommending filing of chargesheet before Hon'ble Court under above sections. Report submitted to ACP, Patel Nagar Sub-Division for supervisory review and approval.\nReports Prepared: Investigation Completion Report, Draft Chargesheet\nSubmitted To: ACP Patel Nagar for approval\nCase Diary Certification: Certified that this case diary contains a true and complete account of investigation conducted by me in case FIR No. 452/2024 PS Rajinder Nagar. All dates, times, and actions are recorded contemporaneously.\nIo Signature: Inspector Suresh Chandra\nSupervisory Remarks: Investigation thorough and complete. Chargesheet approved for filing. - ACP Patel Nagar, 28-11-2024",
